    "body": "I did manage to find a similar issue with bits.Len(), as it also relies on flags. \r\n\r\n```\r\npackage oddsched\r\n\r\nimport (\r\n\t\"math/bits\"\r\n)\r\n\r\nfunc AppendVarint(p []byte, x uint64) []byte {\r\n\tt := [10]byte{\r\n\t\tuint8(x) | 0x80,\r\n\t\tuint8(x>>7) | 0x80,\r\n\t\tuint8(x>>14) | 0x80,\r\n\t\tuint8(x>>21) | 0x80,\r\n\t\tuint8(x>>28) | 0x80,\r\n\t\tuint8(x>>35) | 0x80,\r\n\t\tuint8(x>>42) | 0x80,\r\n\t\tuint8(x>>49) | 0x80,\r\n\t\tuint8(x>>56) | 0x80,\r\n\t\t1,\r\n\t}\r\n\tn := (bits.Len64(x|1) + 6) / 7\r\n\tt[n-1] &= 0x7F\r\n\treturn append(p, t[:n]...)\r\n}\r\n```\r\nThe assembly starts with performing x|1 and a BSR, then goes initialises t, so has to perform another BSRQ to finally compute n.\r\n\r\n```\r\n\tMOVQ\t\"\".x+152(SP), DX\r\n\tMOVQ\tDX, BX\r\n\tORQ\t$1, DX\r\n\tBSRQ\tDX, SI\r\n        ... init t...\r\n   \tBSRQ\tDX, DX\r\n\tMOVQ\t$-1, DX\r\n\tCMOVQEQ\tDX, SI\r\n\tLEAQ\t7(SI), DX\r\n\tMOVQ\t$5270498306774157605, AX\r\n\tMOVQ\tDX, CX\r\n\tIMULQ\tDX\r\n\tSARQ\t$1, DX\r\n\tSARQ\t$63, CX\r\n\tSUBQ\tCX, DX\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n",
